      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral edema or shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects would last a long time. Your patient's kidney and liver function are normal and they have no allergies, so nothing in the information you gave me explains the higher dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily**, a lower starting dose sometimes used in frail or elderly patients.\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intended, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
