      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: amlodipine 50 mg by mouth, once daily.\n\nSince this is well above the usual 10 mg maximum, I added a note to the order. It says the dose is intentional, that you confirmed it, that the specialist recommended it after standard dosing failed, and that it's documented in the chart. The note also suggests close BP and heart rate monitoring.\n\nPharmacy and nursing may call to verify the dose. You may also want to set hold parameters, such as a systolic BP threshold, and plan for monitoring after the first dose. Amlodipine's effects last a long time, so hypotension could come on late and persist."
      }
